Don't kill your walls.

54
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:39,900
You make me realize who I need.

55
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:42,000
I'll be there.

56
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,660
Hold on, the changes somehow.

57
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:46,820
So where are you now?

58
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:50,520
I'll reach you, my dark.

59
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:55,380
The shadows of the earth can lose you so far.

60
00:03:56,400 --> 00:04:04,120
The golden end is too wrong, but I know it's a pain that makes us too human after all.

61
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:07,120
Toin' and see me, a bolder control.

62
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,100
About your precious worth.

63
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:12,080
This scar may respond to your call.

64
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:36,040
Come on, slowpokes, it's time to go.

65
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:36,580
Okay.

66
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:40,220
We're heading out, so you guys hold down the fort, all right?

67
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:40,880
Sure.

68
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:41,940
Have fun.

69
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,060
Bye-bye.

70
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:46,120
See you later.

71
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:49,080
Lunchtime is my favorite time of day.

72
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,740
I'm so hungry.

73
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,360
My stomach's rumbling.

74
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:53,380
Careful now.

75
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:55,900
You're gonna trip over someone if you rush like that.

76
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:58,600
Hey, you.

77
00:04:58,980 --> 00:04:59,440
What's up?

78
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:01,040
Can't you see that I'm reading?

79
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:01,760
Oh, come on.

80
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:02,940
Take a break for a sec.

81
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:04,080
What is with you?

82
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,360
You're being annoying.

83
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:08,480
If we could escape from this place, what would you want to do?

84
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,440
Where would you want to go?

85
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:11,240
Huh?

86
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,560
Did you hit your head or something?

87
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:17,420
We can't escape because the virus would kill us as soon as we got outside.

88
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:19,460
Use your imagination.

89
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:25,120
If we could escape to the outside with the rest of the family, if we could go to a place

90
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:28,440
without any vampires, then don't you think we would have fun?

91
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,580
Without vampires?

92
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:32,440
Yeah.

93
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:33,600
Just us family.

94
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,720
Sure, that sounds great, but it's impossible.

95
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:37,960
You'd be happy?

96
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:39,460
Yeah, of course I would.

97
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:43,420
Then I guess I'd better get busy working on that.

98
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,280
On what?

99
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,200
Mm-mm.

100
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,380
It's a secret.

101
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:49,380
Well, I've got some errands I need to run.

102
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:50,900
Errands?

103
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,440
What do you have to do?

104
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:55,680
If I told you, it'd ruin the surprise.

105
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,340
What a weirdo.

106
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:07,520
Unfortunately, Mika didn't escape the way he thought he would.

107
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:12,020
And it turned out the world beyond was no paradise.

108
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:23,160
We should go meet the others.

109
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,920
But the corporal...

110
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,040
He'll be fine here.

111
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,020
The doctors say he's going to recover.

112
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,400
That's good.

113
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:31,680
I'm glad.

114
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:37,580
Besides, Lieutenant Colonel Gurren has issued some new orders for our squadron.

115
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,600
Gurren's in Shinjuku?

116
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,820
Oh, that's right.

117
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,840
He's reorganizing our troops within the city.

118
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:53,840
The Lieutenant Colonel is already ahead of us at West Shinjuku in Fifth Street.

119
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,960
He's been fighting the vampire's main forces there.

120
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,160
We need to go back him up.

121
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:01,140
The main forces.

122
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:05,100
If we can crush them, then the vampires will be defeated and we'll win this.

123
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:08,080
They're probably thinking the same thing about us.

124
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:11,420
If they crush the Moon Demon Company, victory is theirs.

125
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,580
We should get moving.

126
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,920
Mitsu and the others have probably made it to the defensive line by now.

127
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:21,800
I told you it's not possible.

128
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:27,700
Our orders are to send everyone we've got to the defensive line.

129
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:30,780
If the vampires get through there, Shinjuku will fall.

130
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:33,920
But our troops are going to be wiped out here if we don't help them.

131
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:36,020
So send in the extermination unit.

132
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:38,620
They're teenage kids and there's only three of them.

133
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:41,200
I thought they were supposed to have five members.

134
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,960
