142
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,240
That extermination unit.

143
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,880
Was it the Moon Demon Company?

144
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,940
Um, I don't know.

145
00:08:01,180 --> 00:08:01,540
Maybe.

146
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:02,340
Why?

147
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:03,180
Who are you?

148
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,660
We're part of the Moon Demon...

149
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,300
Wait, you said there were three of them.

150
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,540
Is it a girl and two guys?

151
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:08,620
Yeah.

152
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,920
Are you with them or what?

153
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:12,560
Look, I just need you to tell me where they're fighting.

154
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,660
They're at Shinjuku Central Park.

155
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:15,540
All right.

156
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,120
We're going to go help them.

157
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,420
Send everyone else to the defensive line.

158
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:19,840
Got it?

159
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:20,820
Let's go.

160
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,020
Hey, wait a minute!

161
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:26,960
You're not thinking clearly.

162
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:30,140
You can't even be sure that he was talking about our squad.

163
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:32,960
We can't ignore our orders based on speculation.

164
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:35,240
We're needed as backup.

165
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:36,860
That's our top priority.

166
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:42,620
Even Lieutenant Colonel Gurren will have a hard time going up against the Vampire's strongest forces.

167
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,800
We have to maintain Shinjuku's defensive line.

168
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:48,260
Gurren is counting on us to be there.

169
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,900
So are the rest of his troops.

170
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:13,980
Gurren is counting on us to be there.

171
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:17,060
Yeah.

172
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:17,980
Gurren.

173
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:26,880
Christopher.

174
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:40,460
There's no end to these bloodsuckers.

175
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:44,760
Mito and I can keep them occupied, while you go after the commander.

176
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:47,400
When did you get so good at strategizing?

177
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:48,720
Let's do it!

178
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:57,560
This fight's finally getting interesting.

179
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:01,700
It's a shame that Crowley, the 13th progenitor, isn't here.

180
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:04,700
He would make this a battle truly worthy of the history books.

181
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,960
He's really missing out.

182
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:13,420
Lachis, Rene, round up our men and take down all the humans except for the one in charge.

183
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:16,020
Sir, consider it done.

184
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:27,260
Well, Mika, maybe now I'll finally get a chance to see Cruel Tebysh's favorite servant in action.

185
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:30,260
You must be very thirsty.

186
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:37,520
You and I can kill their pompous leader together.

187
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,260
What do you say?

188
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:43,000
I can do this on my own.

189
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,420
Think so? Then he's all yours.

190
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:48,340
He will regret coming to attack me.

191
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,060
It will be his undoing.

192
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:51,660
My sword!

193
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:56,100
Oh, how intimidating.

194
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:15,760
I think we're almost there, Hugh!

195
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:16,400
Yeah.

196
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:21,480
Thank you.

197
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:23,880
We're coming.

198
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:29,520
Well, we are a family, and it's just like Lieutenant Colonel Gurren told us.

199
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:32,140
We have to protect each other, no matter what.

200
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:36,260
Idiots.

201
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:36,640
What?

202
00:11:37,540 --> 00:11:38,980
That's what he would call you.

203
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:41,020
He probably would.

204
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:44,180
There it is.

205
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:46,000
Shinjuku Central Park.

206
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,600
You're reaching!

207
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:04,580
Behind you!

208
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:04,780
Huh?

209
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:08,580
Damn it!

210
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:34,380
Are we really this week without Shorty and the dumbass backing us up?

211
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:37,420
We can't complete a formation without them.

212
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:43,580
Get ready!

213
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,000
Don't underestimate me!

214
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:50,540
Kimisaki!

215
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:51,420
Want your back?

216
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:53,280
Goodbye!

217
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:58,140
Look, it's you!

218
00:12:58,760 --> 00:12:59,060
Huh?

219
00:12:59,060 --> 00:13:06,640
Don't get distracted on the battlefield, Mitsu.

220
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:15,060
Where are the rest of the vampires?

221
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:17,800
They're all dead, genius.

222
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:20,180
Actually, you just killed the last one of them.

223
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:21,880
Huh?

224
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:31,800
Well, damn, you guys.

225
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,640
Looks like you're pretty amazing after all.

226
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:37,220
You must have forgotten how good I am at killing Vance.

227
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:40,060
Hey, shouldn't you be backing up Gurren?

228
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:41,760
What are you talking about?

229
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:46,200
I heard you were in a tight spot, so I came to make sure you didn't get backed into a corner.

230
00:13:46,580 --> 00:13:47,800
You didn't need to do that.

231
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:52,120
Besides, we said we'd meet you at the defensive line.

232
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:53,600
That was your plan.

233
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:55,940
Sure, that was the plan.

234
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:58,020
But I just thought...

235
00:13:58,020 --> 00:13:59,300
What, that we would fail?

236
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:03,720
Did you honestly think we didn't have the strength and training to take down an enemy platoon?

237
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:09,620
You've got to learn to trust your family.

238
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:17,000
You're right.

239
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:18,440
My bad.

240
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:22,560
Yeah, well, don't go making the same mistake in the future.

241
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:23,560
Okay?

242
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:29,280
Sorry, but if it was to happen again tomorrow, I'd still come running.

243
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:31,020
You what?

244
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:33,120
Did you hear anything I just said?

245
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:36,340
It's not that I don't trust you or think that you're weak.

246
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:38,140
It's just that I care.

247
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:44,020
I'd do it tomorrow, the day after, forever.

248
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,760
What was I thinking?

249
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,800
I must have forgotten what a hardcore dumbass you can be.

250
00:14:50,540 --> 00:14:53,180
You shouldn't bother wasting your breath with him, Komizuki.

251
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:55,300
You can't fix his brand of stupid.

252
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:56,540
You're right.

253
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:59,020
Seems the more we try, the dumber he gets.

254
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:00,280
Oh, come on, guys.

255
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,660
They're just kidding.

256
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:09,660
The sun is finally out.

257
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:13,420
Now that we've cleaned out the park, we should probably catch up with Gurren.

258
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:14,940
Yeah, you're right.

259
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,620
And we can go as a full squad.

260
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,180
Ready, you?

261
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,500
Hell yeah, let's move.

262
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:24,080
We're going to kill every one of those blood-sucking bastards.

263
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:54,060
We're going to kill every one of those blood-sucking bastards.

264
00:15:54,080 --> 00:16:12,560
Well, well, you're a strong one.

265
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,100
A challenge at last.

266
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:17,480
Yes, but not one that you will win.

267
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:25,320
Explode now, Fudomiya O spell.

268
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:47,240
Letting a curse on your head.

269
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,860
I thought that you'd be faster.

270
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:50,480
I evaded the blast.

271
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:55,260
And besides, do you really think old-school spellcraft works on vampires?

272
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,180
Mika, just as I expected.

273
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:02,280
Tremendous power and overconfidence.

274
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:06,280
If you're not careful, that arrogance will get the rug pulled out from under you.

275
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,140
Do you need a hand?

276
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,600
What are you getting at?

277
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,880
There's no way I'll lose against him.

278
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,540
The rug underneath you.

279
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:20,120
You see, our enemies never intended to fight us one-on-one.

280
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:22,040
They've caught on, Shigurei.

281
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:23,140
Kill them.

282
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:24,200
Yes, sir.

283
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:36,320
Goshi, the illusionary spell.

284
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,660
Already on it.

285
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:52,260
And this is checkmate.

286
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:53,580
Vampire!

287
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:01,000
There, Mika.

288
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:02,560
Now you owe me one.

289
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:17,840
Damn.

290
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:19,640
It's worse than I thought.

291
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:24,040
The silver-haired one must be a noble.

292
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:26,180
He's way too strong.

293
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:27,900
Remember, Mika.

294
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:31,000
It's always a mistake to underestimate the livestock.

295
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:35,320
There's nothing honorable about the way these greedy little bloodbags fight.

296
00:18:36,180 --> 00:18:39,700
Although I guess you know all about that as an ex-human yourself.

297
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:40,960
Shut up.

298
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:45,620
Well, we should probably get serious about this.

299
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:46,960
Let's fight together.

300
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:48,500
I don't need your help.

301
00:18:49,140 --> 00:18:51,280
I know what their strategy is now.

302
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:54,780
My sword.

303
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:56,640
Drink more of my blood.

304
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,140
There's that arrogance again.

305
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:04,680
It's an unfortunate holdover from your humanity that's going to get you in trouble one day.

306
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:20,440
Looks like I'll have to take two pills to pull this one off.

307
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,460
Don't risk it, Lieutenant Colonel!

308
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:25,000
Distraction will get you killed, little girl.

309
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,300
Speak for yourself.

310
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:34,960
Oh, wow.

311
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:36,220
Not bad.

312
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:38,920
Please, put the pills away.

313
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:42,300
If you die of shock from taking two of them, then you can't lead us.

314
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,880
But if I don't take them, we'll all end up dead.

315
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:47,280
The clock is ticking.

316
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:50,520
We have to kill them before the pills' effects wear off.

317
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,940
Are you done talking yet?

318
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,120
I want to get this over with.

319
00:19:55,660 --> 00:19:57,520
Well, aren't you a polite vampire?

320
00:19:58,020 --> 00:20:00,060
Would you let us have a little more time to regroup?

321
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:01,620
How much more?

322
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:07,020
It's time for us to take our medicine, so if you could be quiet for 20 seconds or so, we'd...

323
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:12,400
Well, you can't blame a guy for trying.

324
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:16,420
And is it just me, or are you a lot faster than before?

325
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:19,180
I'm not holding anything back from now on.

326
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:23,620
Holding back on the battlefield?

327
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:25,800
Sounds like the strategy of a child.

328
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:28,500
You shouldn't taunt someone stronger than you.

329
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,640
It's not smart!

330
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,320
Damn you.

331
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,320
I guess this is it.

332
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:46,700
Looks like his backup has arrived.

333
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,140
Go on, Mika.

334
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,440
Put the poor man out of his misery.

335
00:20:57,140 --> 00:20:57,980
Not good.

336
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,200
He's been cornered.

337
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:01,600
Quick, everyone, take your pill.

338
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:04,080
We'll save the lieutenant colonel and then retreat.

339
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,540
Let's do this!

340
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:08,040
Yeah.

341
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:11,680
This is the end.

342
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:12,540
Human.

343
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:14,500
Do it, then.

344
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:18,800
Torrent!

345
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:30,320
You damn vampire!

346
00:21:30,780 --> 00:21:32,800
You get away from him right now!

347
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,340
Another reckless human.

348
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,080
What annoying pests.

349
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:44,200
No way is that.

350
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:52,880
You?

351
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:53,620
You?

352
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:56,580
You?

353
00:21:56,580 --> 00:22:26,560
作詞・作曲・編曲 初音ミク

354
00:22:26,580 --> 00:22:56,560
初音ミク

355
00:22:56,580 --> 00:23:26,560
初音ミク

356
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:37,020
Next time on Seraph of the End.

357
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:39,760
Reunion of childhood friends.

